{%- comment -%}
  Popcorn & Freddy — send the Shopify-hosted storefront back to the real site.

  WHY: the site is headless (Cloudflare Pages at popcornfreddy.com); Shopify only
  serves cart/checkout. Checkout's own links — the logo, "continue shopping",
  the login link — point at Shopify's PRIMARY domain, i.e. its templated theme.
  This bounces every theme-rendered page to popcornfreddy.com, keeping the
  customer's market so an AT buyer lands on /at and a US buyer on /us.

  Checkout is NOT affected: Shopify does not load theme.liquid inside checkout.

  WHERE: Shopify admin → Online Store → Themes → ⋯ → Edit code → layout/theme.liquid
  Paste this block IMMEDIATELY after the opening <head> tag, before anything else.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script>
  (function () {
    var SITE = 'https://popcornfreddy.com';
    // Shopify's market country → our locale prefix. Anything else → bare domain,
    // where /api/geo picks the prefix.
    var MAP = { AT: '/at/', DE: '/de/', CH: '/ch/', US: '/us/' };
    var country = {{ localization.country.iso_code | json }};
    var target = SITE + (MAP[country] || '/');
    // replace(), not href: no Shopify page in the customer's back history.
    window.location.replace(target);
  })();
</script>
